{"text": "MARLIN SHARE OF MARKET\nJANUARY, 1997\n\nPERFORMANCE OVERVIEW\n* Shifts in Industry price tiers from December to January remained very small.\n\n* As expected, RJR's overall retail performance stabilized in January (-.02 share\npoints month-to-month) as competitive pressure eased relative to year-end\nactivity. Reflecting national roll-out and associated introductory buy-some\nactivity, CAMEL Menthol reached a share of .24 for the period, an increase of\n+.14 versus December. CAMEL, in total, was up .07 share points. Despite the\nCAMEL increase, RJR FP was down slightly as WINSTON performance\nsoftened in January (-.12 month-to-month). Our Savings business was up\nslightly as FORSYTH posted an increase (+.05) and the balance of RJR\nSavings was stable.\n\nPM's experienced a slight share loss in total in January (-.11 share points) as\ntheir Savings business declined (due largely to Basic) and there was no\noffsetting FP growth. With no major promotional support during the period,\nMarlboro's share was essentially flat (-.06).\n\n* Lorillard regained the share lost in December, with an increase of 14 share\npoints in January. Strong Newport performance as well as contributions from\nthe expansion of Maverick were responsible for the company's gain.\n\n* BAT was down significantly (-.84) reflecting the sale of several Savings brands\n(including Montclair) to Commonwealth\n\nOUTLOOK\n\n* We don't expect to see any improvement in our overall retail performance over\nthe next couple of months and may experience slight share declines, at least\non total FP. Competitive activities at retail will increase in February/March,\nincluding a lighter offer on Marlboro in February and aggressive discounting\non Marlboro and Basic in March. Both CAMEL and DORAL should benefit\nfrom buysome offers (Base CAMEL in February, DORAL in February/March).\nHowever, it is likely that, at least for February, WINSTON's trend will remain\nsoft.\n\nfP98 Lees\n\nRJR0000000517022348\n70022 1307",
